NOTE 0 Ideal thin lens f = 100, stop on the lens, EPD 20 (f/5), at unit-ish conjugates: the object sits
NOTE 0 200 mm in front and the flat image 200 mm behind. The OBJECT SURFACE IS CURVED, radius -300, so a
NOTE 0 field point of height h lies at its sag, not on the vertex plane, and its image is out of focus on
NOTE 0 the flat image plane. For a Lambertian object that does not matter: the illuminance at an image
NOTE 0 point is set by the cone of directions reaching it, which here is the cone to the stop disk.
NOTE 0 Exact answer: Foote's disk formula at the chief ray's image height (Gardner Eq. 7).
NOTE 0 Fields are object heights 0 / 30 / 60 mm.
